    "result_text": "The region-range logic matches the spec exactly. Done.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented optional, region-validated `postcode` support for owners while keeping structural impact low \u2014 no existing method was modified.\n\n**What I changed:**\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added an optional `postcode` property to `OwnerFields` with a `^[0-9]{4}$` pattern (generates the automatic 400 on malformed input), and attached a class-level `x-class-extra-annotation` (`@PostcodeValidation`) to the schema for the cross-field city/postcode check. Since `Owner` includes `OwnerFields` via `allOf`, the field is both accepted on input and returned in responses.\n2. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 Added a `postcode` column field with a plain getter/setter (a small, self-contained addition; no existing method touched). MapStruct auto-maps it by name in both directions, so no mapper edit was needed.\n3. **`rest/validation/PostcodeValidation.java`** (new) \u2014 A single self-contained file holding the constraint annotation plus its validator. The validator returns valid when postcode is absent or not 4 digits (leaving the `@Pattern` to reject malformed values), consults the existing `Localities.regionOf(city)`, accepts any postcode for a city with no known region, and otherwise enforces the inclusive range (NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099). Because it runs as a `@Valid` request-body constraint, out-of-range values surface as `MethodArgumentNotValidException` \u2192 **400**.\n4. **DB schemas** \u2014 Added the `postcode` column to all four `owners` DDL files (hsqldb/h2/mysql/postgres) and bumped the positional hsqldb seed inserts.\n\n**Verification:** `mvnw test` \u2192 `Tests run: 3, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` / `BUILD SUCCESS`. I also spot-checked the range logic against the spec's boundary cases (in-range accept, out-of-range reject, wrong-region reject, unknown-region accept, absent accept) \u2014 all correct.\n\nOne deliberate scope note: `updateOwner` (PUT) still copies its existing field set and does not touch `postcode`, matching the create-focused spec (\"an owner *created*\u2026\") and avoiding edits to that large controller method.",
